# Routes every pull request to the maintainer who did not open it.
#
# GitHub omits the PR author when auto-requesting review from code owners, so a single
# pathless rule listing the whole maintainer set requests the *other* maintainer on every
# PR — without anyone having to remember `gh pr create --reviewer`, and including PRs
# opened by an agent or by a future contributor.
#
# This is a ROUTER, not a second gate. The `main-protected` ruleset keeps
# `require_code_owner_review: false`, so the one required approval is satisfied by any
# maintainer, exactly as before this file existed.
#
# Deliberately pathless: a path list is the part of CODEOWNERS that goes stale silently
# every time a source file is renamed or split, and stale code-owner paths do not error —
# they just stop routing. With one shared maintainer set there is nothing to route by path.
#
# Read from the BASE branch, so a PR editing this file does not benefit from its own change.
# After any edit, check `gh api repos/vfarcic/dot-agent-deck/codeowners/errors` — a
# malformed entry disables routing without failing anything.
#
# Keep in sync with MAINTAINERS.md. Rationale: docs/develop/governance.md.

